11. POINT MODEL
A point represents a position in project coordinates.
Point2
Point3
A point shall not be treated interchangeably with a vector.
The distinction must be enforced within the geometry API.

12. TRANSFORMS
The geometry engine shall support:
translation
rotation
reflection
scaling
coordinate transformation
Architectural model elements shall normally use:
translation
rotation
Scaling of physical building elements shall not occur through arbitrary graphical transforms.
Dimensional changes must modify semantic parameters.

13. TOLERANCE MODEL
Geometric equality shall use an explicit tolerance.
Initial default:
GEOMETRIC_TOLERANCE = 0.01 mm
The tolerance shall be configurable by subsystem where necessary.
Examples:
point equality
line intersection
parallelism
coplanarity
coincidence
Exact floating-point equality shall not be used for geometric comparison.

