49. COMMAND VALIDATION
Before execution:
verify authorization
verify project
verify revision
verify target objects
verify parameters
verify constraints
verify object state
verify model version
If validation fails, no model mutation occurs.

50. COMMAND PLANNING
Commands shall first produce an execution plan.
Example:
MOVE WALL
becomes:
1. Identify wall
2. Resolve wall geometry
3. Identify hosted openings
4. Identify affected spaces
5. Identify affected drawings
6. Identify affected validation rules
7. Calculate proposed geometry
8. Check constraints
9. Produce mutation plan
The plan may then be approved or executed according to command policy.

